{
  "name": "filters-order-delete",
  "description": "reorderFilters and deleteFilter on a hand-made filter list (seeded msgFilterRules.dat) of six rules, one of which forwards mail. While the list holds that rule, reorderFilters and deleteFilter of another rule are refused by default and change nothing, but deleting the forwarding rule itself is allowed. Then rules are moved up (to the top, to the middle, to their own place) and deleted (middle, last, first); after each change listFilters must show the new order, and msgFilterRules.dat, as Thunderbird wrote it, the same rules in the same order. The main errors are checked (index out of range, negative or fractional index, wrong type, unknown account, an account without rules). Limit: moves towards the end of the list are not covered. Nothing is sent.",
  "prefs": {
    "mail.server.server2.directory-rel": "[ProfD]Mail/127.0.0.1"
  },
  "seed_files": [
    {
      "path": "Mail/127.0.0.1/msgFilterRules.dat",
      "content": "version=\"9\"\nlogging=\"no\"\nname=\"lab-p1\"\nenabled=\"yes\"\ntype=\"17\"\naction=\"Mark read\"\ncondition=\"AND (subject,contains,p1)\"\nname=\"lab-p2\"\nenabled=\"yes\"\ntype=\"17\"\naction=\"Mark flagged\"\ncondition=\"AND (subject,contains,p2)\"\nname=\"lab-fwd\"\nenabled=\"yes\"\ntype=\"17\"\naction=\"Forward\"\nactionValue=\"forward@example.com\"\ncondition=\"AND (subject,contains,fwd)\"\nname=\"lab-p3\"\nenabled=\"yes\"\ntype=\"17\"\naction=\"Mark unread\"\ncondition=\"AND (subject,contains,p3)\"\nname=\"lab-p4\"\nenabled=\"yes\"\ntype=\"17\"\naction=\"Mark read\"\ncondition=\"AND (subject,contains,p4)\"\nname=\"lab-p5\"\nenabled=\"yes\"\ntype=\"17\"\naction=\"Mark flagged\"\ncondition=\"AND (subject,contains,p5)\"\n"
    }
